-- title:
--   Quotient H/⟨ c⟩ ≅ I from a surjection with index-matched cyclic kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $U$ be a finite commutative group, $G$ a group, and $\Psi : U \to G$ a surjective group homomorphism. Let $c \in U$ satisfy $\Psi(c) = 1$, and suppose the numerical condition $\operatorname{card} G = [U : \langle c \rangle]$, where $\langle c \rangle =$ `Subgroup.zpowers c` is the subgroup generated by the integral powers of $c$ and the index is taken in $U$. Let $H \le U$ be a subgroup with $c \in H$, and let $I \le G$ be a subgroup such that for every $u \in U$ one has $\Psi(u) \in I$ if and only if $u \in H$. The conclusion asserts that the type of multiplicative isomorphisms from the quotient of $H$ by the subgroup generated by the integral powers of the element $c$, viewed as an element of $H$ via the membership $c \in H$, to the subgroup $I$ is nonempty; that is, there exists an isomorphism of groups $H/\langle c \rangle \cong I$. (The conclusion is stated as nonemptiness of the type of isomorphisms rather than as a designated isomorphism.)
--
--   This is an application of the first isomorphism theorem together with a Lagrange index count, which forces $\ker \Psi$ to be exactly the cyclic subgroup $\langle c\rangle$. It is used in the analysis of the modular curve $X_1 \to X_0$ at supersingular points, to present the relevant inertia subgroup of diamond operators as a quotient of a group of units by the subgroup generated by a distinguished element.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Subgroup_nonempty_quotient_zpowers_mulEquiv_of_forall_apply_mem_iff.lean

